        "id": 1475908
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-12-11T11:37:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "RT1715 chip is designed during TCPCI spec rev 0.6 changing to rev 1.0. And rt1715 CC_STATUS register is defined as rev 0.6 spec as following,\n    1. BIT 7, 6: reserved\n       BIT 5: DRP_STATUS - 0b: TCPC has stopped toggling or ROLE_CONTROL_DRP \u003d00)\n       BIT 4: DRP_RESULT - 0b: TCPC is presenting Rp,1b: the TCPC is presenting Rd:\n               (this bit is only valid if the TCPC was a DRP and has stopped DRP toggling)\n       BIT 3..2: CC2_STATUS\n       BIT 1..0: CC1 STATUS\n    \nSo,we need to do following steps to get cc1, cc2 state.\n    1. Read the ROLE_CTRL.DRP state first \n    2. If ROLE_CTRL.DRP \u003d 1, we can get current CC Rp/ Rd state from CC_STATUS.DRP_RESULT \n          ROLE_CTRL.DRP \u003d 0, we can get current CC Rp/ Rd state from ROLE_CTRL.CC1\n    3. According to current CC present Rp/ Rd state, then we could finally get the cc1, cc2 \n       state",
      "parentUuid": "e5fd4902_3ca3f146",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 130,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 132,
        "endChar": 64
      },
      "revId": "712b9438a9c6774cc98250678091dcb7926cc2ee",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
